Z||000000||Philphine||08-27-2001||08:39 AM||||<BR>my chopper project has a short shifter in it already. since i haven't driven it i don't know if this will be a problem, but i noticed when i pull it back to the 2nd and 4th positions it seems like the shift boot being squashed dowm on the shorter shaft keeps it from engaging well. <P>has anyone driving with one noticed any problems? do you modify the boot (cut some material away or something)? maybe in the future i should be looking for one of those gated plates?<P>last, if you have a gated plate, dose it "feel" ok? in a way it seems like it might hinder things too if you don't shift cleanly (like hitting the sides or slamming into the cross in the H pattern). thanks for any help. ||||reg||1
