Z||000003||Tryxalon||08-27-2001||09:54 PM||||Lots of people like the shortened shifter. One poster even commented that if you don't like the shortened shifter you must have "weak girly arms"<BR>-- a comment that my gorilla-armed self found greatly amusing. <P>I tried it - made one from a bone yard shifter and used it for about 5 weeks.  Hated it -- always seemed to be banging the shifts.  Gave the shortened shifter to a guy I work with -- he put it in his girl friends Red 84 and <u>she </u>loves it.  Go figure.  <P>I like the stock shifter with my 85 SE 4cyl with Isuzu 5speed. <p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||08-28-2001||08:18 AM||||I have rodney's short shifter and his leather boot that comes with it.  No problem at all with the boot hindering the shifting.||||reg||1
